-- title:
--   Existence of a coefficient ring for a residual Hecke eigensystem
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ be a natural number, let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a local domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with finite residue field. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S)`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and let $\theta \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ be a ring homomorphism into the residue field. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6): the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ spanned by the forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are integers is the whole space. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $T$ carrying a commutative ring structure which is local, Noetherian and adically complete for its maximal ideal, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure whose structure map is a local homomorphism and makes $T$ a finite free $\mathcal{O}$-module, with $T/\mathfrak{m}_T$ finite, and of a ring homomorphism $\pi \colon \mathbb{T} \to T$ such that: the residue of $\pi(t)$ in $T/\mathfrak{m}_T$ equals the image of $\theta(t)$ under the induced map of residue fields, for every $t \in \mathbb{T}$; the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the range of $\pi$ is all of $T$; every ring homomorphism $\chi \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}$ whose reduction is $\theta$ factors through $\pi$ via some $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\psi \colon T \to \mathcal{O}$; and the composite $\mathcal{O} \to T \to T/\mathfrak{m}_T$ is surjective. Only existence is asserted; no uniqueness and no Galois representation over $T$.
--
--   This packages the coefficient ring of a residual Hecke eigensystem $\theta$ — classically the localisation of $\mathcal{O} \otimes \mathbb{T}$ at the maximal ideal cut out by $\theta$ — as a complete local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, generated by the images of the Hecke operators, through which all $\mathcal{O}$-valued eigensystems lifting $\theta$ factor, and with residue field that of $\mathcal{O}$. It is used in the construction of the Hecke-side Galois representation datum attached to a residually modular curve of given level.
